[Fact:negativeBases:The ↑ operator and negative bases]
Expressions such as 'X↑Y' give an 'Invalid argument' error when X is negative,
even when Y is an integer. For example:

<code>PRINT (-1)↑2</code>

This is because the #R$3851 routine computes the value as EXP (Y*LN X), and
LN X is undefined for negative values of X.
